From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vi: drop frames that fail the CSI bridge checks

isp_err_chk finds a frame whose line or frame size differs from the
setting, a CSI bridge FIFO overflow or a DMA error. It counts the error
and wakes the error handler thread, which resets and restarts the pipe,
and it returns -1. The interrupt handler ignored that result and went on
to the frame done handling, which queues the frame as a good one: a
frame damaged on the receiver's MIPI link reached the encoders.

Sipeed's driver for the same SoC returns from the interrupt handler on
every isp_err_chk failure (LicheeRV-Nano-Build, osdrv/interdrv/v2/vi/
chip/mars/vi.c). This returns when the error handler is resetting the
pipe (the size and FIFO errors wake it), after the CMDQ status is
cleared; the DMA and over-maximum errors, which wake nothing, go on as
before so the pipe is not left without a restart. Both trees read and
clear the interrupt status at the top of the handler.

---
diff --git a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c
--- a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c
+++ b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vi.c
@@ -8552,8 +8552,20 @@
 			ctx->isp_pipe_cfg[raw_num].dg_info.bdg_chn_debug[i] = ispblk_csibdg_chn_dbg(ctx, raw_num, i);
 	}
 
-	isp_err_chk(vdev, ctx, cbdg_0_sts[0], cbdg_1_sts[0], cbdg_0_sts[1], cbdg_1_sts[1],
-		cbdg_0_sts[2], cbdg_1_sts[2]);
+	/* A frame that failed the CSI bridge checks while the error handler
+	 * thread is resetting the pipe (isp_err_chk woke it for a short or
+	 * long line or frame or a FIFO overflow) is not passed on: its frame
+	 * done would queue it as a good frame. The thread restarts the pipe.
+	 * Sipeed's driver returns on every isp_err_chk failure; errors that do
+	 * not wake the thread (DMA, frame size over the maximum) go on as
+	 * before here, as nothing would restart the pipe after them. */
+	const u32 frame_err = isp_err_chk(vdev, ctx, cbdg_0_sts[0], cbdg_1_sts[0],
+		cbdg_0_sts[1], cbdg_1_sts[1], cbdg_0_sts[2], cbdg_1_sts[2]);
+
+	if (frame_err == (u32)-1 && atomic_read(&vdev->isp_err_handle_flag)) {
+		_isp_cmdq_done_chk(vdev, top_sts_2.bits.CMDQ_INT);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	//if (top_sts.bits.INT_DMA_ERR)
 	//	vi_pr(VI_ERR, "DMA error\n");
